"John H." <JohnWH@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> I like the idea of extending credit cards to actually, you know,
> provide credit-related services, but:
> 1. All successful characters eventually reach a place where they can
> walk over shopkeepers with little effort.  Thought would have to be put
> into avoiding making things like credit cloning worse with working
> credit cards.

I don't see how that would be worse than using a bag which are much
more common than credit cards. 

You can't get more gold out of a shopkeeper than the amount he has.

> 2. There's already a lack of things to use money on in the game.  The
> historical use for money (dating back to Rogue) is score.  More
> recently have come into being shops, protection and bribery.  Later in
> the game, however, all these uses except protection become meaningless
> where, ideally, players should never lack for things to spend cash on.
> Credit cards used in this manner would make it easier to collect and
> maintain wealth, but it doesn't really need to be made easier --
> instead, money needs to be more valuable.

I think there are already enough possibilities to spend ones gold.
You can buy stuff in shops, ask the Oracle for direction or donate to
priests.

After all the goal of NetHack is not to get the biggest pile of gold.

